f 1080 "$H$ and $K$ only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186160990 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186160990 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d9a2f5e8-88f2-5ca7-829a-bde5ff808860" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186160991 #edb/ref 1080 "$J$ only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186160991 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186160991 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e7a99bd4-fb67-538c-9ece-a4608cb1871a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186160992 #edb/ref 1080 "$J$ and $K$ only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186160992 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186160992 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fca7d285-ba33-51b7-8ce8-27bc0b3b6983" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186160993 #edb/ref 1080 "$H$ and $J$ only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186160993 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186160993 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1f4a9a25-8245-5a1f-bdb8-7661bfd56e83" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161776 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8168" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161776 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following could be matrices of quadratic forms defined on $\\mathbb{R}^2?$\n\n![](images/52/528416f6f9bd58e04afc6df73ddffbe1e8645f1e94fc7113d1458fb806f08713.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161776 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "122fd33e-5ef4-5200-9c72-67f40f3b8ca0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161776 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that every quadratic form defined on $\\mathbb{R}^2$ has an associated $2 \\times 2$ symmetric matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- $L$ *cannot* be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on $\\mathbb{R}^2$ since it's a $3 \\times 3$ matrix (not $2 \\times 2$).\n\n- $M$ *cannot* be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on $\\mathbb{R}^2.$  Although it's a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, $M$ is not symmetric since $m_{12} \\neq m_{21}.$\n\n- $N$ could be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on $\\mathbb{R}^2$ since it is a $2 \\times 2$ symmetric matrix.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$N$ only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161777 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8169" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161777 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/f8/f85f2ebf91733fa3b5f0b6080da27be0ee4333ee2b7b27ab3fac2dad1acb2d41.svg)\nGiven the matrix $A$ above, evaluate the quadratic form $Q(\\mathbf{x}) = \\mathbf{x}^T \\! A \\mathbf{x}$ when ![](images/81/815a776cae60244113513dc20183d05caeece6aaef807fd65e5c4ac819f2d4d3.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161777 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d782c826-1111-5c83-98b6-220856d74b41" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161777 #edb/ref 1074 "Substituting ![](images/e8/e8a68c7428583d7df9f7fb18faf50f315192475e2f9bb12d051ccc1fda5638a3.svg) into the expression for $Q(\\mathbf{x}),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}^{T}\\,Ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 23\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =86.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161778 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8170" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161778 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/0a/0aa2d0bbe2e39ba23901b5157466b4099c1f2552d9a34de9af6387975c59e1cb.svg)\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which expression represents the corresponding quadratic form $\\mathbf{x}^T \\! A \\mathbf{x}$ in terms of the components of ![](images/37/37cee7d28f0085ee70cefd5cb9ded630e38ffb3ca26523c320df13d09cde09e8.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161778 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f3be44df-f059-5e92-b279-644fe1eb0985" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161778 #edb/ref 1074 "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry $a_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term $a_{ij}x_i x_j$ in the expression of the quadratic form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =-1{x}_{1}{x}_{1}+(1){x}_{1}{x}_{2}+(1){x}_{2}{x}_{1}+-1{x}_{2}{x}_{2} \\\\  & =-{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =-{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a quadratic form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}(-{x}_{1}+{x}_{2})+{x}_{2}({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =-{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161779 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8171" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161779 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/36/36f35d430db979991c566198b6126c940d2b5e35682edbabffb458a77b991488.svg)\nThe matrix of the quadratic form ![](images/16/16124e0080293b4221a1fbe668c41d2c293ebe6780025a433530a48ef7047063.svg) is given above. What is the value of ![](images/43/43b267893b1bca2af9d56014fddd4b93a381f8e2c827cb88e6ba2269f1425432.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161779 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9ed75397-5920-5326-a5b9-7537e30f0a85" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161779 #edb/ref 1074 "Since the matrix of the quadratic form must be symmetric, we rewrite our expression as follows:\n\n![](images/38/38d71b4d0e2e6e4e271e04889292fc77209655fd96accd7ab94358839527c381.svg)\n\nNotice that to get a symmetric matrix, we must do the following splits:\n\n- we split the coefficient of ![](images/3c/3cd51b9ca52bf7654f66792b03bd448a08b1122b07fb9028abf3cf9eb317691e.svg) between the entries ![](images/04/041786e547d7190e7dc272dcce677ae110c98a1c27601d701527c08a27ce069f.svg) and\n\n- we split the coefficient of ![](images/82/824c1904e6a2dbe749c4a8c6dba76e5f1f3470e44c549f9fe472f11b871b1fe5.svg) between the entries ![](images/e2/e2035cd0dc43c754085c2be1daf4394ebe91d59706bc609c2398323dc160edee.svg)\n\nSo, the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form is\n\n![](images/ff/ffc81faf6d2f06bbe8d74cd6b8fc69e9cd1d38a330f492bf925441633ca283e5.svg)\n\nTherefore, ![](images/5d/5db60b1276b1838de62d9a1fa07bdb79930a293720bc5e88ab3113863282afeb.svg) ![](images/af/af43e412255aa69feb8f127bcba2b8aa43eb5d5efb12d692f4f4e2d49c035a98.svg) and ![](images/18/187bf10c65391a58d6b69f746f7f2c4cf2939b3beacfc02c15cef309875c3b57.svg) Finally, \n![](images/af/af56151e2bfb52d48f7b45d954f8c91cbaa1831fe024245667f4f4d721c87e6f.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161984 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050021 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161984 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186162592 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161984 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186162616 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161984 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186272168 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161984 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186357639 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161984 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186357640 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161984 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186357641 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161984 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186491113 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161984 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying Matrices of Quadratic Forms" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161984 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186161776 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161984 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "e62e458d-0724-5dbe-b448-b79404f279f9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161985 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050407 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161985 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186162593 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161985 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186162594 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161985 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186272172 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161985 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186357643 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161985 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186357644 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161985 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186357646 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161985 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186357